+	# This is a very minimal implementation of the subdirectory creation logic
+	# in ServerInstanceDir.h. This implementation is only meant to make the unit
+	# tests pass. For production systems one should pre-create the temp
+	# directory with ServerInstanceDir.h.
+	#
+	# The name is derived from the process ID, so another user on the machine
+	# can prepare it before this process starts. The directory is therefore
+	# created here and, when it already exists, only used after checking that
+	# it is a plain directory which belongs to this process and which nobody
+	# else may write to. A link is refused even when it resolves to such a
+	# directory: every later write through the returned path would follow it
+	# again, so nothing below a prepared name can be considered ours.
+	def self.prepare_tmpdir(dir)
+		created = false
+		begin
+			Dir.mkdir(dir, 0700)
+			created = true
+		rescue Errno::EEXIST
+			# The name is taken; inspect what is there below.
+		rescue Errno::ENOENT
+			# The parent directories don't exist yet. Create them, but still
+			# create the last component ourselves so that it is ours.
